From 1e7b66960c4b526d0b8f573242d306030759c70d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:42:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Backport MinGW's scoped LLVM 23 ABI alias compatibility

Backport MinGW commits 6c6368cb4a682b5c8b95a61d088efce453074cf4,
01290efca885ae171f427ddbd338d21ac265a658, and
b43f781b916e8170b66bc4c6784123e53b283f8a to v14.0.0.
Adapt only four include-context differences and add a WORKAROUND
reference to issue #61 with the upstream fix and removal condition.

The positive compiler regression builds the actual MinGW runtime
objects, then requires an unrelated alias mismatch to fail at its
expected diagnostic. No global warning flag is relaxed.

Verification: tools/build-warnings/mingw/check.sh
--platforms=//:windows_x86_64_gnullvm --keep_going reproduces
-Wattribute-alias before the backport and passes afterwards.
Maintained just fmt-check and just bazel-lock-check pass.
Logs: mingw-runtime-alias-{red,green}.log and
mingw-alias-{fmt,lock}-check.log in llvm-toolchain task evidence.

Use two lines of innermost context to avoid copying existing source trailing whitespace into the nested patch. Reconstructed native Git trees are byte-identical before and after this context-only change.
---
 MODULE.bazel                                  |   1 +
 patches/llvm_mingw_attribute_alias.patch      | 412 ++++++++++++++++++
 tools/build-warnings/mingw/BUILD.bazel        |   9 +
 .../mingw/attribute_alias_warning.c           |   5 +
 tools/build-warnings/mingw/check.sh           |  20 +
 5 files changed, 447 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 patches/llvm_mingw_attribute_alias.patch
 create mode 100644 tools/build-warnings/mingw/BUILD.bazel
 create mode 100644 tools/build-warnings/mingw/attribute_alias_warning.c
 create mode 100755 tools/build-warnings/mingw/check.sh

